/-!
# The conductor and primitive associate of a good Hecke eigenform

Every good Hecke eigenform `f` of level `N` and nebentypus `χ` (`EigenformAwayFromLevel N k`)
determines a unique divisor `M ∣ N` and newform `g : Newform M k` whose nebentypus induces `χ`
modulo `N` and whose Hecke eigenvalues at the primes not dividing `N` equal those of `f`; moreover,
`f` lies in the oldspace generated by `g`, the span of the level-raises `V_d g` with `d * M ∣ N`
(Diamond–Shurman, Theorem 5.8.3 and Proposition 5.8.4; Miyake, Corollary 4.6.20). This file names
`M` as `EigenformAwayFromLevel.conductor`, the **conductor** of the eigensystem of `f`, and `g` as
`EigenformAwayFromLevel.primitiveAssociate`, Miyake's **primitive form** attached to `f`, and
develops their theory.

## Mathematical overview

* **Character descent and all good indices.** Because `g.χ` pulls back to `f.χ` along
  `(ZMod N)ˣ → (ZMod M)ˣ`, the zero-extended Dirichlet character `MulChar.ofUnitHom f.χ` is the
  level-raise of `g.dirichletLift`; in particular it factors through `f.conductor`, so its
  character conductor divides `f.conductor`, and when `f.χ` is primitive `f.conductor = N`. By
  `EigenformAwayFromLevel.eigenvalue_eq_of_comp_unitsMap_eq_of_forall_prime`, equality of
  eigenvalues propagates from good primes to every index `n` coprime to `N`.
* **Universal divisibility and the new/old dichotomy.** Among divisors `M' ∣ N`, `f` arises from
  level `M'` — meaning `f` lies in `∑_{d * M' ∣ N} V_d S_k(Γ₁(M'))` — if and only if
  `f.conductor ∣ M'`. Consequently a good Hecke eigenform is never mixed: it lies in the new
  subspace precisely when `f.conductor = N` (in which case `f = a₁(f) • g`), and in the old
  subspace precisely when `f.conductor < N`.
* **Cross-level comparison of primitive associates.** Across two arbitrary levels `N₁` and `N₂`,
  two good Hecke eigenforms of weight `k` have the same conductor and the same primitive associate
  if and only if their eigenvalues agree at all common good indices outside a finite set, with no
  nebentypus hypothesis: agreement at large primes `p` and their squares `p²` recovers the
  nebentypus values via `χ(p) = (λ_p² - λ_{p²}) / p^{k-1}`, Dirichlet's theorem equates the lifted
  characters, and cross-level strong multiplicity one equates the primitive associates. When the
  nebentypes are already known to agree on a common multiple of the levels, agreement at the common
  good primes outside a finite set suffices.
* **Stability under level-raising and oldspace combinations.** Bundling a nonzero cusp form in the
  span of `{V_d f | d * M ∣ N}` via `EigenformAwayFromLevel.ofMemSpanLevelRaise` — in particular
  the bundled level-raise `EigenformAwayFromLevel.levelRaise` — preserves the conductor and
  primitive associate of `f`. Specialising to `V₁ g + c • V_d g` for a newform `g` and `1 < d`
  produces, for every `c : ℂ`, a normalised good Hecke eigenform of conductor `M` and primitive
  associate `g` whose `d`-th Fourier coefficient is `a_d(g) + c`, showing that the good eigensystem
  leaves bad-prime coefficients unconstrained.

## Main definitions (in `HeckeRing.GL2`)

* `EigenformAwayFromLevel.conductor`: the conductor `M ∣ N` of a good Hecke eigenform.
* `EigenformAwayFromLevel.primitiveAssociate`: the unique newform of level `f.conductor` attached
  to `f`.

## Main results (in `HeckeRing.GL2`)

* `EigenformAwayFromLevel.conductor_dvd`,
  `EigenformAwayFromLevel.primitiveAssociate_χ_comp_unitsMap`,
  `EigenformAwayFromLevel.conductor_ofUnitHom_χ_dvd_conductor`,
  `EigenformAwayFromLevel.primitiveAssociate_eigenvalue`,
  `EigenformAwayFromLevel.mem_span_levelRaise_primitiveAssociate`: defining properties.
* `EigenformAwayFromLevel.level_eq_conductor_and_coe_eq_primitiveAssociate`,
  `EigenformAwayFromLevel.conductor_eq_and_coe_primitiveAssociate_eq_iff_exists_finset`,
  `EigenformAwayFromLevel.conductor_eq_and_coe_primitiveAssociate_eq_iff_of_comp_unitsMap_eq`:
  uniqueness and cross-level characterisation of equal primitive associates.
* `Newform.conductor_toEigenformAwayFromLevel`,
  `EigenformAwayFromLevel.conductor_eq_self_iff_mem_cuspFormsNew`,
  `EigenformAwayFromLevel.conductor_lt_self_iff_mem_cuspFormsOld`,
  `EigenformAwayFromLevel.conductor_dvd_iff_mem_iSup_levelRaise`,
  `EigenformAwayFromLevel.isLeast_conductor`: new/old dichotomy and universal level-divisibility.
* `EigenformAwayFromLevel.conductor_ofMemSpanLevelRaise`,
  `EigenformAwayFromLevel.conductor_levelRaise`,
  `Newform.exists_eigenformAwayFromLevel_qExpansion_coeff_eq`: oldspace stability and bad-prime
  non-rigidity.

## References

* [F. Diamond and J. Shurman, *A first course in modular forms*][diamondshurman2005],
  Theorem 5.8.3 and Proposition 5.8.4.
* [T. Miyake, *Modular forms*][miyake1989], Theorem 4.6.19 and Corollary 4.6.20.
-/

public section

open Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup UpperHalfPlane CongruenceSubgroup ZMod TauCeti

open scoped MatrixGroups ModularForm

namespace HeckeRing.GL2

variable {N M L : ℕ} {k : ℤ}

namespace EigenformAwayFromLevel

/-! ### The conductor and primitive associate -/

/-- **The conductor of a good Hecke eigenform** (Miyake, Corollary 4.6.20; Diamond–Shurman,
Theorem 5.8.3 and Proposition 5.8.4): the unique divisor `M` of `N` carrying a newform whose
nebentypus induces `f.χ` modulo `N` and whose good-prime Hecke eigenvalues agree with those of `f`.
Uniqueness (`level_eq_conductor_and_coe_eq_primitiveAssociate`) makes it independent of any choice
and invariant under raising the ambient level. -/
noncomputable def conductor [NeZero N] (f : EigenformAwayFromLevel N k) : ℕ :=
  f.exists_newform_mem_span_levelRaise.choose

/-- The conductor of a good Hecke eigenform is nonzero. -/
instance [NeZero N] (f : EigenformAwayFromLevel N k) : NeZero f.conductor :=
  f.exists_newform_mem_span_levelRaise.choose_spec.choose

/-- The conductor of a good Hecke eigenform is positive. -/
theorem conductor_pos [NeZero N] (f : EigenformAwayFromLevel N k) : 0 < f.conductor :=
  NeZero.pos f.conductor

/-- **The conductor divides the ambient level.** -/
theorem conductor_dvd [NeZero N] (f : EigenformAwayFromLevel N k) : f.conductor ∣ N :=
  f.exists_newform_mem_span_levelRaise.choose_spec.choose_spec.choose

/-- The conductor is at most the ambient level. -/
theorem conductor_le_self [NeZero N] (f : EigenformAwayFromLevel N k) : f.conductor ≤ N :=
  Nat.le_of_dvd (NeZero.pos N) f.conductor_dvd

/-- **Every good Hecke eigenform of level `1` has conductor `1`.** -/
@[simp]
theorem conductor_level_one (f : EigenformAwayFromLevel 1 k) : f.conductor = 1 :=
  Nat.dvd_one.mp f.conductor_dvd

/-- **The primitive associate of a good Hecke eigenform** (Miyake's *primitive form* attached to
`f`, Corollary 4.6.20; Diamond–Shurman, Proposition 5.8.4): the unique newform of level
`f.conductor` whose nebentypus induces `f.χ` modulo `N` and whose Hecke eigenvalues away from `N`
are those of `f`. -/
noncomputable def primitiveAssociate [NeZero N] (f : EigenformAwayFromLevel N k) :
    Newform f.conductor k :=
  f.exists_newform_mem_span_levelRaise.choose_spec.choose_spec.choose_spec.choose

private theorem primitiveAssociate_spec [NeZero N] (f : EigenformAwayFromLevel N k) :
    f.primitiveAssociate.χ.comp (unitsMap f.conductor_dvd) = f.χ ∧
    (∀ (p : ℕ) (hp : p.Prime) (hpN : Nat.Coprime p N),
      f.primitiveAssociate.eigenvalue ⟨p, hp.pos⟩ (hpN.coprime_dvd_right f.conductor_dvd) =
        f.eigenvalue ⟨p, hp.pos⟩ hpN) ∧
    f.toCuspForm ∈ Submodule.span ℂ {G : CuspForm ((Gamma1 N).map (mapGL ℝ)) k |
      ∃ (d : ℕ) (_ : NeZero d) (h : d * f.conductor ∣ N),
        CuspForm.levelRaise d (Gamma1_map_le_conjAct_scaleGL_of_dvd h)
          f.primitiveAssociate.toCuspForm = G} ∧
    ∀ (M' : ℕ) (_ : NeZero M') (hM' : M' ∣ N) (g' : Newform M' k),
      g'.χ.comp (unitsMap hM') = f.χ →
      (∀ (p : ℕ) (hp : p.Prime) (hpN : Nat.Coprime p N),
        g'.eigenvalue ⟨p, hp.pos⟩ (hpN.coprime_dvd_right hM') =
          f.eigenvalue ⟨p, hp.pos⟩ hpN) →
      M' = f.conductor ∧ ⇑g'.toCuspForm = ⇑f.primitiveAssociate.toCuspForm :=
  f.exists_newform_mem_span_levelRaise.choose_spec.choose_spec.choose_spec.choose_spec

/-- **The nebentypus of the primitive associate induces that of `f` modulo `N`.** -/
@[simp]
theorem primitiveAssociate_χ_comp_unitsMap [NeZero N] (f : EigenformAwayFromLevel N k)
    (h : f.conductor ∣ N) :
    f.primitiveAssociate.χ.comp (unitsMap h) = f.χ :=
  f.primitiveAssociate_spec.1

/-- Reading the nebentypus of the primitive associate at any multiple `L` of `N` agrees with
reading `f.χ` there. -/
theorem primitiveAssociate_χ_comp_unitsMap_of_dvd [NeZero N] (f : EigenformAwayFromLevel N k)
    (hNL : N ∣ L) (h : f.conductor ∣ L) :
    f.primitiveAssociate.χ.comp (unitsMap h) = f.χ.comp (unitsMap hNL) := by
  rw [← unitsMap_comp f.conductor_dvd hNL, ← MonoidHom.comp_assoc,
    f.primitiveAssociate_χ_comp_unitsMap]

/-- **Raising the Dirichlet character of the primitive associate to level `N` gives the
zero-extended nebentypus of `f`.** -/
@[simp]
theorem changeLevel_primitiveAssociate_dirichletLift [NeZero N] (f : EigenformAwayFromLevel N k)
    (h : f.conductor ∣ N) :
    DirichletCharacter.changeLevel h f.primitiveAssociate.dirichletLift =
      MulChar.ofUnitHom f.χ := by
  rw [← DirichletCharacter.toUnitHom_inj,
    f.primitiveAssociate.changeLevel_dirichletLift_toUnitHom h,
    MulChar.toUnitHom_eq, MulChar.ofUnitHom_eq, Equiv.apply_symm_apply,
    f.primitiveAssociate_χ_comp_unitsMap]

/-- **The nebentypus of `f` factors through its conductor.** -/
theorem factorsThrough_conductor [NeZero N] (f : EigenformAwayFromLevel N k) :
    DirichletCharacter.FactorsThrough
      (MulChar.ofUnitHom f.χ : DirichletCharacter ℂ N) f.conductor := by
  rw [← f.changeLevel_primitiveAssociate_dirichletLift f.conductor_dvd]
  exact DirichletCharacter.changeLevel_factorsThrough _ f.conductor_dvd

-- Not `@[simp]`: `MulChar.ofUnitHom_eq` rewrites `MulChar.ofUnitHom` on the left-hand side.
/-- The character conductor of `f.χ` agrees with that of its primitive associate. -/
theorem conductor_ofUnitHom_χ_eq [NeZero N] (f : EigenformAwayFromLevel N k) :
    DirichletCharacter.conductor (MulChar.ofUnitHom f.χ : DirichletCharacter ℂ N) =
      f.primitiveAssociate.dirichletLift.conductor := by
  rw [← f.changeLevel_primitiveAssociate_dirichletLift f.conductor_dvd,
    DirichletCharacter.conductor_changeLevel]

/-- **The conductor of the nebentypus divides the conductor of the eigenform.** -/
theorem conductor_ofUnitHom_χ_dvd_conductor [NeZero N] (f : EigenformAwayFromLevel N k) :
    DirichletCharacter.conductor (MulChar.ofUnitHom f.χ : DirichletCharacter ℂ N) ∣
      f.conductor := by
  rw [f.conductor_ofUnitHom_χ_eq]
  exact f.primitiveAssociate.dirichletLift.conductor_dvd_level

/-- **A good Hecke eigenform of primitive nebentypus has conductor equal to the ambient level.** -/
theorem conductor_eq_of_isPrimitive [NeZero N] (f : EigenformAwayFromLevel N k)
    (hχ : DirichletCharacter.IsPrimitive (MulChar.ofUnitHom f.χ : DirichletCharacter ℂ N)) :
    f.conductor = N := by
  have hdvd := f.conductor_ofUnitHom_χ_dvd_conductor
  rw [DirichletCharacter.isPrimitive_def] at hχ
  rw [hχ] at hdvd
  exact Nat.dvd_antisymm f.conductor_dvd hdvd

/-- At every prime `p ∤ N`, the eigenvalue of the primitive associate equals that of `f`. -/
theorem primitiveAssociate_eigenvalue_prime [NeZero N] (f : EigenformAwayFromLevel N k)
    {p : ℕ} (hp : p.Prime) (hpN : Nat.Coprime p N) :
    f.primitiveAssociate.eigenvalue ⟨p, hp.pos⟩ (hpN.coprime_dvd_right f.conductor_dvd) =
      f.eigenvalue ⟨p, hp.pos⟩ hpN :=
  f.primitiveAssociate_spec.2.1 p hp hpN

-- Not `@[simp]`: the proof `hn` does not appear on the left-hand side, so `simpNF` rejects it.
/-- **At every index `n` coprime to `N`, the eigenvalue of the primitive associate equals that of
`f`.** -/
theorem primitiveAssociate_eigenvalue [NeZero N] (f : EigenformAwayFromLevel N k) (n : ℕ+)
    (hm : Nat.Coprime (n : ℕ) f.conductor) (hn : Nat.Coprime (n : ℕ) N) :
    f.primitiveAssociate.eigenvalue n hm = f.eigenvalue n hn :=
  eigenvalue_eq_of_comp_unitsMap_eq_of_forall_prime f.primitiveAssociate.toEigenformAwayFromLevel f
    f.conductor_dvd (f.primitiveAssociate_χ_comp_unitsMap f.conductor_dvd)
    (fun _ hp hpN ↦ f.primitiveAssociate_eigenvalue_prime hp hpN) n hm hn

/-- **At every index `n` coprime to `N`, the `n`-th Fourier coefficient of the primitive associate
is the `n`-th eigenvalue of `f`.** -/
theorem qExpansion_coeff_primitiveAssociate [NeZero N] (f : EigenformAwayFromLevel N k) (n : ℕ+)
    (hn : Nat.Coprime (n : ℕ) N) :
    (qExpansion 1 f.primitiveAssociate.toCuspForm).coeff (n : ℕ) = f.eigenvalue n hn := by
  rw [f.primitiveAssociate.qExpansion_coeff_eq_eigenvalue n (hn.coprime_dvd_right f.conductor_dvd)]
  exact f.primitiveAssociate_eigenvalue n _ hn

/-- At every index `n` coprime to `N`, `a_n(f) = a_n(f.primitiveAssociate) * a₁(f)`. -/
theorem qExpansion_coeff_eq_primitiveAssociate_mul_coeff_one [NeZero N]
    (f : EigenformAwayFromLevel N k) (n : ℕ+) (hn : Nat.Coprime (n : ℕ) N) :
    (qExpansion 1 f.toCuspForm).coeff (n : ℕ) =
      (qExpansion 1 f.primitiveAssociate.toCuspForm).coeff (n : ℕ) *
        (qExpansion 1 f.toCuspForm).coeff 1 := by
  rw [f.qExpansion_coeff_primitiveAssociate n hn,
    f.qExpansion_coeff_eq_eigenvalue_mul_coeff_one n hn]

/-- For a normalised good Hecke eigenform (`a₁(f) = 1`), the Fourier coefficients at all indices
coprime to `N` agree with those of its primitive associate. -/
theorem qExpansion_coeff_eq_primitiveAssociate [NeZero N] (f : EigenformAwayFromLevel N k)
    (h₁ : (qExpansion 1 f.toCuspForm).coeff 1 = 1) (n : ℕ+) (hn : Nat.Coprime (n : ℕ) N) :
    (qExpansion 1 f.toCuspForm).coeff (n : ℕ) =
      (qExpansion 1 f.primitiveAssociate.toCuspForm).coeff (n : ℕ) := by
  rw [f.qExpansion_coeff_eq_primitiveAssociate_mul_coeff_one n hn, h₁, mul_one]

/-- **A good Hecke eigenform lies in the oldspace generated by its primitive associate**: the span
of the level-raises `V_d g` with `d * f.conductor ∣ N` (Diamond–Shurman, Theorem 5.8.3 and
Proposition 5.8.4). -/
theorem mem_span_levelRaise_primitiveAssociate [NeZero N] (f : EigenformAwayFromLevel N k) :
    f.toCuspForm ∈ Submodule.span ℂ {G : CuspForm ((Gamma1 N).map (mapGL ℝ)) k |
      ∃ (d : ℕ) (_ : NeZero d) (h : d * f.conductor ∣ N),
        CuspForm.levelRaise d (Gamma1_map_le_conjAct_scaleGL_of_dvd h)
          f.primitiveAssociate.toCuspForm = G} :=
  f.primitiveAssociate_spec.2.2.1

/-! ### Uniqueness and cross-level comparison of primitive associates -/

/-- **Uniqueness of the conductor and primitive associate** (Miyake, Theorem 4.6.19 and Corollary
4.6.20). Let `L` be a common multiple of `N` and `M`. Any newform `g` of level `M` whose nebentypus
agrees with `f.χ` modulo `L` and whose prime eigenvalues agree with those of `f` at all primes
`p ∤ L` outside a finite set `S` has level `f.conductor` and is the same function on `ℍ` as
`f.primitiveAssociate`. -/
theorem level_eq_conductor_and_coe_eq_primitiveAssociate [NeZero N] [NeZero M] [NeZero L]
    (f : EigenformAwayFromLevel N k) (g : Newform M k) (hNL : N ∣ L) (hML : M ∣ L)
    (hχ : g.χ.comp (unitsMap hML) = f.χ.comp (unitsMap hNL)) {S : Finset ℕ}
    (h : ∀ (p : ℕ) (hp : p.Prime) (hpL : Nat.Coprime p L), p ∉ S →
      g.eigenvalue ⟨p, hp.pos⟩ (hpL.coprime_dvd_right hML) =
        f.eigenvalue ⟨p, hp.pos⟩ (hpL.coprime_dvd_right hNL)) :
    M = f.conductor ∧ ⇑g.toCuspForm = ⇑f.primitiveAssociate.toCuspForm := by
  have hcL : f.conductor ∣ L := f.conductor_dvd.trans hNL
  refine Newform.level_eq_and_coe_eq_of_comp_unitsMap_eq g f.primitiveAssociate hML hcL hχ
    (f.primitiveAssociate_χ_comp_unitsMap_of_dvd hNL hcL) (S := S) fun p hp hpL hpS ↦ ?_
  exact (h p hp hpL hpS).trans
    (f.primitiveAssociate_eigenvalue_prime hp (hpL.coprime_dvd_right hNL)).symm

/-- **Uniqueness of the conductor and primitive associate at divisor levels.** A newform `g` of
level `M ∣ N` whose nebentypus induces `f.χ` modulo `N` and whose prime eigenvalues agree with
those of `f` at all primes `p ∤ N` outside a finite set `S` has `M = f.conductor` and coincides
with `f.primitiveAssociate`. -/
theorem level_eq_conductor_and_coe_eq_primitiveAssociate_of_dvd [NeZero N] [NeZero M]
    (f : EigenformAwayFromLevel N k) (g : Newform M k) (hMN : M ∣ N)
    (hχ : g.χ.comp (unitsMap hMN) = f.χ) {S : Finset ℕ}
    (h : ∀ (p : ℕ) (hp : p.Prime) (hpN : Nat.Coprime p N), p ∉ S →
      g.eigenvalue ⟨p, hp.pos⟩ (hpN.coprime_dvd_right hMN) = f.eigenvalue ⟨p, hp.pos⟩ hpN) :
    M = f.conductor ∧ ⇑g.toCuspForm = ⇑f.primitiveAssociate.toCuspForm :=
  f.level_eq_conductor_and_coe_eq_primitiveAssociate g dvd_rfl hMN
    (by simpa only [unitsMap_self, MonoidHom.comp_id] using hχ) h

/-- **Good eigenvalues outside a finite set determine the lifted nebentypus across levels.** If two
good Hecke eigenforms `f₁` and `f₂` of the same weight `k` at arbitrary levels `N` and `M` have
equal eigenvalues at all common good indices outside a finite set `S`, then their zero-extended
nebentypes agree at all but finitely many primes, so their nebentypes induce the same character
modulo every common multiple `L` of `N` and `M`. -/
theorem χ_comp_unitsMap_eq_of_forall_notMem_eigenvalue_eq [NeZero N] [NeZero M] [NeZero L]
    (f₁ : EigenformAwayFromLevel N k) (f₂ : EigenformAwayFromLevel M k)
    (hNL : N ∣ L) (hML : M ∣ L) {S : Finset ℕ}
    (h : ∀ (n : ℕ+) (hnN : Nat.Coprime (n : ℕ) N) (hnM : Nat.Coprime (n : ℕ) M),
      (n : ℕ) ∉ S → f₁.eigenvalue n hnN = f₂.eigenvalue n hnM) :
    f₁.χ.comp (unitsMap hNL) = f₂.χ.comp (unitsMap hML) := by
  have hχ := Newform.χ_comp_unitsMap_eq_of_forall_notMem_qExpansion_coeff_eq
    f₁.primitiveAssociate f₂.primitiveAssociate
    (f₁.conductor_dvd.trans hNL) (f₂.conductor_dvd.trans hML) (S := S) fun n hnL hnS ↦ by
      have hnN := hnL.coprime_dvd_right hNL
      have hnM := hnL.coprime_dvd_right hML
      rw [f₁.qExpansion_coeff_primitiveAssociate n hnN,
        f₂.qExpansion_coeff_primitiveAssociate n hnM]
      exact h n hnN hnM hnS
  rwa [f₁.primitiveAssociate_χ_comp_unitsMap_of_dvd hNL,
    f₂.primitiveAssociate_χ_comp_unitsMap_of_dvd hML] at hχ

/-- **Two good Hecke eigenforms with compatible nebentypes and prime eigenvalues agreeing outside a
finite set have the same conductor and primitive associate.** -/
theorem conductor_eq_and_coe_primitiveAssociate_eq_of_forall_notMem_prime_eigenvalue_eq
    [NeZero N] [NeZero M] [NeZero L]
    (f₁ : EigenformAwayFromLevel N k) (f₂ : EigenformAwayFromLevel M k)
    (hNL : N ∣ L) (hML : M ∣ L)
    (hχ : f₁.χ.comp (unitsMap hNL) = f₂.χ.comp (unitsMap hML)) {S : Finset ℕ}
    (h : ∀ (p : ℕ) (hp : p.Prime) (hpN : Nat.Coprime p N) (hpM : Nat.Coprime p M),
      p ∉ S → f₁.eigenvalue ⟨p, hp.pos⟩ hpN = f₂.eigenvalue ⟨p, hp.pos⟩ hpM) :
    f₁.conductor = f₂.conductor ∧
      ⇑f₁.primitiveAssociate.toCuspForm = ⇑f₂.primitiveAssociate.toCuspForm := by
  refine f₂.level_eq_conductor_and_coe_eq_primitiveAssociate f₁.primitiveAssociate hML
    (f₁.conductor_dvd.trans hNL)
    ((f₁.primitiveAssociate_χ_comp_unitsMap_of_dvd hNL _).trans hχ)
    (S := S ∪ N.primeFactors) fun p hp hpL hpS ↦ ?_
  rw [Finset.mem_union, not_or] at hpS
  have hpN : Nat.Coprime p N := hp.coprime_iff_not_dvd.mpr fun hd ↦
    hpS.2 (Nat.mem_primeFactors.mpr ⟨hp, hd, NeZero.ne N⟩)
  exact (f₁.primitiveAssociate_eigenvalue_prime hp hpN).trans
    (h p hp hpN (hpL.coprime_dvd_right hML) hpS.1)

/-- If two good Hecke eigenforms have the same primitive associate on `ℍ`, their eigenvalues agree
at every index coprime to both ambient levels. -/
theorem eigenvalue_eq_of_coe_primitiveAssociate_eq [NeZero N] [NeZero M]
    {f₁ : EigenformAwayFromLevel N k} {f₂ : EigenformAwayFromLevel M k}
    (hcoe : ⇑f₁.primitiveAssociate.toCuspForm = ⇑f₂.primitiveAssociate.toCuspForm)
    (n : ℕ+) (hnN : Nat.Coprime (n : ℕ) N) (hnM : Nat.Coprime (n : ℕ) M) :
    f₁.eigenvalue n hnN = f₂.eigenvalue n hnM := by
  rw [← f₁.qExpansion_coeff_primitiveAssociate n hnN,
    ← f₂.qExpansion_coeff_primitiveAssociate n hnM, hcoe]

/-- **Characterisation of equal primitive associates under compatible nebentypes.** When `f₁` and
`f₂` have nebentypes agreeing modulo a common multiple `L` of their levels, they have equal
conductors and equal primitive associates if and only if their prime eigenvalues agree outside a
finite set. -/
theorem conductor_eq_and_coe_primitiveAssociate_eq_iff_of_comp_unitsMap_eq
    [NeZero N] [NeZero M] [NeZero L]
    (f₁ : EigenformAwayFromLevel N k) (f₂ : EigenformAwayFromLevel M k)
    (hNL : N ∣ L) (hML : M ∣ L)
    (hχ : f₁.χ.comp (unitsMap hNL) = f₂.χ.comp (unitsMap hML)) :
    (f₁.conductor = f₂.conductor ∧
        ⇑f₁.primitiveAssociate.toCuspForm = ⇑f₂.primitiveAssociate.toCuspForm) ↔
      ∃ S : Finset ℕ, ∀ (p : ℕ) (hp : p.Prime) (hpN : Nat.Coprime p N) (hpM : Nat.Coprime p M),
        p ∉ S → f₁.eigenvalue ⟨p, hp.pos⟩ hpN = f₂.eigenvalue ⟨p, hp.pos⟩ hpM :=
  ⟨fun h ↦ ⟨∅, fun p hp hpN hpM _ ↦
    eigenvalue_eq_of_coe_primitiveAssociate_eq h.2 ⟨p, hp.pos⟩ hpN hpM⟩,
   fun ⟨_, hS⟩ ↦
    conductor_eq_and_coe_primitiveAssociate_eq_of_forall_notMem_prime_eigenvalue_eq f₁ f₂ hNL hML
      hχ hS⟩

/-- **Two good Hecke eigenforms whose good eigenvalues agree outside a finite set have the same
conductor and primitive associate, with no nebentypus hypothesis.** -/
theorem conductor_eq_and_coe_primitiveAssociate_eq_of_forall_notMem_eigenvalue_eq
    [NeZero N] [NeZero M] (f₁ : EigenformAwayFromLevel N k) (f₂ : EigenformAwayFromLevel M k)
    {S : Finset ℕ}
    (h : ∀ (n : ℕ+) (hnN : Nat.Coprime (n : ℕ) N) (hnM : Nat.Coprime (n : ℕ) M),
      (n : ℕ) ∉ S → f₁.eigenvalue n hnN = f₂.eigenvalue n hnM) :
    f₁.conductor = f₂.conductor ∧
      ⇑f₁.primitiveAssociate.toCuspForm = ⇑f₂.primitiveAssociate.toCuspForm := by
  set L := Nat.lcm N M
  have : NeZero L := ⟨Nat.lcm_ne_zero (NeZero.ne N) (NeZero.ne M)⟩
  have hNL : N ∣ L := Nat.dvd_lcm_left N M
  have hML : M ∣ L := Nat.dvd_lcm_right N M
  exact conductor_eq_and_coe_primitiveAssociate_eq_of_forall_notMem_prime_eigenvalue_eq f₁ f₂
    hNL hML (χ_comp_unitsMap_eq_of_forall_notMem_eigenvalue_eq f₁ f₂ hNL hML h)
    (S := S) fun p hp hpN hpM hpS ↦ h ⟨p, hp.pos⟩ hpN hpM hpS

/-- **Characterisation of equal primitive associates across arbitrary levels.** Two good Hecke
eigenforms `f₁` and `f₂` of the same weight at levels `N` and `M` have the same conductor and the
same primitive associate on `ℍ` if and only if their good eigenvalues agree outside a finite set. -/
theorem conductor_eq_and_coe_primitiveAssociate_eq_iff_exists_finset [NeZero N] [NeZero M]
    (f₁ : EigenformAwayFromLevel N k) (f₂ : EigenformAwayFromLevel M k) :
    (f₁.conductor = f₂.conductor ∧
        ⇑f₁.primitiveAssociate.toCuspForm = ⇑f₂.primitiveAssociate.toCuspForm) ↔
      ∃ S : Finset ℕ, ∀ (n : ℕ+) (hnN : Nat.Coprime (n : ℕ) N) (hnM : Nat.Coprime (n : ℕ) M),
        (n : ℕ) ∉ S → f₁.eigenvalue n hnN = f₂.eigenvalue n hnM :=
  ⟨fun h ↦ ⟨∅, fun n hnN hnM _ ↦ eigenvalue_eq_of_coe_primitiveAssociate_eq h.2 n hnN hnM⟩,
   fun ⟨_, hS⟩ ↦ conductor_eq_and_coe_primitiveAssociate_eq_of_forall_notMem_eigenvalue_eq f₁ f₂ hS⟩

/-- **Rigidity of the good eigensystem across levels.** Two good Hecke eigenforms of the same
weight have the same conductor and primitive associate if and only if their eigenvalues agree at
*every* index coprime to both ambient levels. -/
theorem conductor_eq_and_coe_primitiveAssociate_eq_iff_forall_eigenvalue_eq [NeZero N] [NeZero M]
    (f₁ : EigenformAwayFromLevel N k) (f₂ : EigenformAwayFromLevel M k) :
    (f₁.conductor = f₂.conductor ∧
        ⇑f₁.primitiveAssociate.toCuspForm = ⇑f₂.primitiveAssociate.toCuspForm) ↔
      ∀ (n : ℕ+) (hnN : Nat.Coprime (n : ℕ) N) (hnM : Nat.Coprime (n : ℕ) M),
        f₁.eigenvalue n hnN = f₂.eigenvalue n hnM :=
  ⟨fun h n hnN hnM ↦ eigenvalue_eq_of_coe_primitiveAssociate_eq h.2 n hnN hnM,
   fun h ↦ conductor_eq_and_coe_primitiveAssociate_eq_of_forall_notMem_eigenvalue_eq f₁ f₂
    (S := ∅) fun n hnN hnM _ ↦ h n hnN hnM⟩

/-- **Minimality of the conductor across levels.** If `f` shares its good eigenvalues outside a
finite set with any good Hecke eigenform `h` of level `M`, then `f.conductor ∣ M`. -/
theorem conductor_dvd_of_forall_notMem_eigenvalue_eq [NeZero N] [NeZero M]
    (f : EigenformAwayFromLevel N k) (h : EigenformAwayFromLevel M k) {S : Finset ℕ}
    (heig : ∀ (n : ℕ+) (hnN : Nat.Coprime (n : ℕ) N) (hnM : Nat.Coprime (n : ℕ) M),
      (n : ℕ) ∉ S → f.eigenvalue n hnN = h.eigenvalue n hnM) :
    f.conductor ∣ M := by
  rw [(conductor_eq_and_coe_primitiveAssociate_eq_of_forall_notMem_eigenvalue_eq f h heig).1]
  exact h.conductor_dvd

end EigenformAwayFromLevel

/-! ### Newforms, the new/old dichotomy, and universal level-divisibility -/

namespace Newform

/-- **The conductor of a newform is its own level.** -/
@[simp]
theorem conductor_toEigenformAwayFromLevel [NeZero N] (g : Newform N k) :
    g.toEigenformAwayFromLevel.conductor = N :=
  (g.toEigenformAwayFromLevel.level_eq_conductor_and_coe_eq_primitiveAssociate_of_dvd g dvd_rfl
    (by simp) (S := ∅) fun _ _ _ _ ↦ rfl).1.symm

/-- **The primitive associate of a newform is the newform itself.** -/
@[simp]
theorem coe_primitiveAssociate_toEigenformAwayFromLevel [NeZero N] (g : Newform N k) :
    ⇑g.toEigenformAwayFromLevel.primitiveAssociate.toCuspForm = ⇑g.toCuspForm :=
  (g.toEigenformAwayFromLevel.level_eq_conductor_and_coe_eq_primitiveAssociate_of_dvd g dvd_rfl
    (by simp) (S := ∅) fun _ _ _ _ ↦ rfl).2.symm

end Newform

namespace EigenformAwayFromLevel

/-- When a newform `g` of level `M` shares the nebentypus and good-prime eigenvalues of `f` and
`M = N`, `f` is `a₁(f) • g` and therefore lies in the new subspace. -/
private theorem eq_coeff_one_smul_and_mem_cuspFormsNew_of_level_eq [NeZero N] [NeZero M]
    (f : EigenformAwayFromLevel N k) (g : Newform M k) (hMN : M ∣ N)
    (hχ : g.χ.comp (unitsMap hMN) = f.χ)
    (hp : ∀ (p : ℕ) (hp : p.Prime) (hpN : Nat.Coprime p N),
      g.eigenvalue ⟨p, hp.pos⟩ (hpN.coprime_dvd_right hMN) = f.eigenvalue ⟨p, hp.pos⟩ hpN)
    (h : M = N) :
    ⇑f.toCuspForm = (qExpansion 1 f.toCuspForm).coeff 1 • ⇑g.toCuspForm ∧
      f.toCuspForm ∈ cuspFormsNew N k := by
  subst h
  have hgχ : g.χ = f.χ := by simpa only [unitsMap_self, MonoidHom.comp_id] using hχ
  have hline := g.eq_qExpansion_coeff_one_smul_of_forall_prime_heckeTCuspNat_eq_smul
    (F := f.toCuspForm) (hgχ ▸ f.mem_charSpace) fun p hpr hpM ↦ by
      rw [hp p hpr hpM]
      exact f.heckeTCuspNat_eq_eigenvalue_smul hpr hpM
  exact ⟨(congrArg DFunLike.coe hline).trans (FunLike.coe_smul _ _),
    hline ▸ Submodule.smul_mem _ _ g.isNew⟩

/-- If `f.conductor = N`, `f` is the `a₁(f)`-multiple of its primitive associate. -/
theorem coe_toCuspForm_eq_coeff_one_smul_primitiveAssociate_of_conductor_eq [NeZero N]
    (f : EigenformAwayFromLevel N k) (h : f.conductor = N) :
    ⇑f.toCuspForm = (qExpansion 1 f.toCuspForm).coeff 1 • ⇑f.primitiveAssociate.toCuspForm :=
  (eq_coeff_one_smul_and_mem_cuspFormsNew_of_level_eq f f.primitiveAssociate f.conductor_dvd
    (f.primitiveAssociate_χ_comp_unitsMap f.conductor_dvd)
    (fun _ hp hpN ↦ f.primitiveAssociate_eigenvalue_prime hp hpN) h).1

/-- Every level-raise from a proper divisor `f.conductor ≠ N` lands in `cuspFormsOld N k`. -/
private theorem mem_cuspFormsOld_of_conductor_ne [NeZero N] (f : EigenformAwayFromLevel N k)
    (hne : f.conductor ≠ N) : f.toCuspForm ∈ cuspFormsOld N k := by
  refine Submodule.span_le.mpr ?_ f.mem_span_levelRaise_primitiveAssociate
  rintro _ ⟨d, _, hd, rfl⟩
  exact levelRaise_mem_cuspFormsOld hd hne k f.primitiveAssociate.toCuspForm

/-- **A good Hecke eigenform lies in the new subspace if and only if its conductor equals the
ambient level.** -/
theorem conductor_eq_self_iff_mem_cuspFormsNew [NeZero N] (f : EigenformAwayFromLevel N k) :
    f.conductor = N ↔ f.toCuspForm ∈ cuspFormsNew N k := by
  constructor
  · exact fun h ↦ (eq_coeff_one_smul_and_mem_cuspFormsNew_of_level_eq f f.primitiveAssociate
      f.conductor_dvd (f.primitiveAssociate_χ_comp_unitsMap f.conductor_dvd)
      (fun _ hp hpN ↦ f.primitiveAssociate_eigenvalue_prime hp hpN) h).2
  · intro hnew
    by_contra hne
    exact f.ne_zero ((Submodule.disjoint_def.mp (disjoint_cuspFormsOld_cuspFormsNew N k))
      f.toCuspForm (f.mem_cuspFormsOld_of_conductor_ne hne) hnew)

/-- **A good Hecke eigenform lies in the old subspace if and only if its conductor is not the
ambient level.** -/
theorem conductor_ne_self_iff_mem_cuspFormsOld [NeZero N] (f : EigenformAwayFromLevel N k) :
    f.conductor ≠ N ↔ f.toCuspForm ∈ cuspFormsOld N k :=
  ⟨f.mem_cuspFormsOld_of_conductor_ne, fun hold h ↦ f.ne_zero
    ((Submodule.disjoint_def.mp (disjoint_cuspFormsOld_cuspFormsNew N k)) f.toCuspForm hold
      (f.conductor_eq_self_iff_mem_cuspFormsNew.mp h))⟩

/-- **A good Hecke eigenform lies in the old subspace if and only if its conductor is strictly
smaller than the ambient level.** -/
theorem conductor_lt_self_iff_mem_cuspFormsOld [NeZero N] (f : EigenformAwayFromLevel N k) :
    f.conductor < N ↔ f.toCuspForm ∈ cuspFormsOld N k := by
  rw [← f.conductor_ne_self_iff_mem_cuspFormsOld]
  exact ⟨ne_of_lt, fun hne ↦ lt_of_le_of_ne f.conductor_le_self hne⟩

/-- If `f` lies in the span of level-raised newforms from levels dividing `M`, then
`f.conductor ∣ M`, by independence of nebentypus spaces and joint good-prime eigenspaces. -/
private theorem conductor_dvd_of_mem_span_newform [NeZero N]
    (f : EigenformAwayFromLevel N k)
    (hspan : f.toCuspForm ∈ Submodule.span ℂ {G : CuspForm ((Gamma1 N).map (mapGL ℝ)) k |
      ∃ (M' c : ℕ) (_ : NeZero M') (_ : NeZero c) (hc : c * M' ∣ N),
        M' ∣ M ∧ ∃ g' : Newform M' k,
          CuspForm.levelRaise c (Gamma1_map_le_conjAct_scaleGL_of_dvd hc) g'.toCuspForm = G}) :
    f.conductor ∣ M := by
  by_contra hndvd
  let ι := {p : ℕ // p.Prime ∧ Nat.Coprime p N}
  let T : ι → Module.End ℂ (CuspForm ((Gamma1 N).map (mapGL ℝ)) k) := fun p ↦
    heckeTCuspNat k p.val (_hn := ⟨p.property.1.ne_zero⟩)
  let af : ι → ℂ := fun p ↦ f.eigenvalue ⟨p.val, p.property.1.pos⟩ p.property.2
  -- Split into `f.χ`-forms with good eigensystem `≠ af` and forms of nebentypus `≠ f.χ`.
  have hmem : f.toCuspForm ∈
      ((⨆ (a : ι → ℂ) (_ : a ≠ af), ⨅ p : ι, (T p).eigenspace (a p)) ⊓
        cuspFormCharSpace k f.χ) ⊔
      ⨆ (ψ : (ZMod N)ˣ →* ℂˣ) (_ : ψ ≠ f.χ), cuspFormCharSpace k ψ := by
    refine Submodule.span_le.mpr ?_ hspan
    rintro _ ⟨M', c, _, _, hcN, hM'M, g', rfl⟩
    have hM'N : M' ∣ N := dvd_of_mul_left_dvd hcN
    have hchar := CuspForm.levelRaise_mem_cuspFormCharSpace_of_dvd hcN g'.χ g'.mem_charSpace
    by_cases hg'χ : g'.χ.comp (unitsMap hM'N) = f.χ
    · refine Submodule.mem_sup_left ⟨?_, hg'χ ▸ hchar⟩
      let ag' : ι → ℂ := fun p ↦
        g'.eigenvalue ⟨p.val, p.property.1.pos⟩ (p.property.2.coprime_dvd_right hM'N)
      have hne : ag' ≠ af := fun heq ↦ hndvd <| by
        have := (f.level_eq_conductor_and_coe_eq_primitiveAssociate_of_dvd g' hM'N hg'χ
          (S := ∅) fun p hp hpN _ ↦ congrFun heq ⟨p, hp, hpN⟩).1
        exact this ▸ hM'M
      refine Submodule.mem_iSup_of_mem ag' (Submodule.mem_iSup_of_mem hne ?_)
      exact (Submodule.mem_iInf _).mpr fun p ↦ Module.End.mem_eigenspace_iff.mpr
        (g'.heckeTCuspNat_levelRaise_eq_eigenvalue_smul hcN p.property.1 p.property.2)
    · exact Submodule.mem_sup_right (Submodule.mem_iSup_of_mem _
        (Submodule.mem_iSup_of_mem hg'χ hchar))
  obtain ⟨s, hs, t, ht, hst⟩ := Submodule.mem_sup.mp hmem
  have htχ : t ∈ cuspFormCharSpace k f.χ := by
    have := Submodule.sub_mem _ f.mem_charSpace hs.2
    rwa [← hst, add_sub_cancel_left] at this
  have ht0 : t = 0 :=
    (Submodule.disjoint_def.mp (iSupIndep_def.mp (iSupIndep_cuspFormCharSpace k) f.χ)) t htχ ht
  rw [ht0, add_zero] at hst
  have hfeig : f.toCuspForm ∈ ⨅ p : ι, (T p).eigenspace (af p) :=
    (Submodule.mem_iInf _).mpr fun p ↦ Module.End.mem_eigenspace_iff.mpr
      (f.heckeTCuspNat_eq_eigenvalue_smul p.property.1 p.property.2)
  exact f.ne_zero ((Submodule.disjoint_def.mp (iSupIndep_iInf_eigenspace T af)) f.toCuspForm
    hfeig (hst ▸ hs.1))

/-- **Universal level-divisibility property of the conductor.** For a divisor `M ∣ N`, a good Hecke
eigenform `f` of level `N` lies in `∑_{d * M ∣ N} V_d S_k(Γ₁(M))` if and only if
`f.conductor ∣ M`. -/
theorem conductor_dvd_iff_mem_iSup_levelRaise [NeZero N] [NeZero M]
    (f : EigenformAwayFromLevel N k) (hMN : M ∣ N) :
    f.conductor ∣ M ↔
      f.toCuspForm ∈ ⨆ (d : ℕ) (hd : d * M ∣ N),
        haveI : NeZero d := NeZero.of_dvd (dvd_of_mul_right_dvd hd)
        LinearMap.range
          (CuspForm.levelRaiseₗ (k := k) d (Gamma1_map_le_conjAct_scaleGL_of_dvd hd)) := by
  constructor
  · intro hCM
    refine Submodule.span_le.mpr ?_ f.mem_span_levelRaise_primitiveAssociate
    rintro _ ⟨d, _, hd, rfl⟩
    -- Factor `d = d₂ * d₁` across `(M / f.conductor) * (N / M)` so `V_d = V_{d₁} ∘ V_{d₂}`
    -- steps through level `M`.
    obtain ⟨q, hM⟩ := hCM
    obtain ⟨r, hN⟩ := hMN
    have hdqr : d ∣ q * r := (Nat.mul_dvd_mul_iff_left f.conductor_pos).mp <| by
      rwa [← mul_assoc, ← hM, ← hN, mul_comm f.conductor d]
    obtain ⟨d₂, d₁, hd₂q, hd₁r, rfl⟩ := exists_dvd_and_dvd_of_dvd_mul hdqr
    have hd₂M : d₂ * f.conductor ∣ M := hM ▸ mul_comm f.conductor q ▸ mul_dvd_mul_right hd₂q _
    have hd₁N : d₁ * M ∣ N := hN ▸ mul_comm M r ▸ mul_dvd_mul_right hd₁r _
    have : NeZero d₁ := NeZero.of_dvd (dvd_of_mul_right_dvd hd₁N)
    have : NeZero d₂ := NeZero.of_dvd (dvd_of_mul_right_dvd hd₂M)
    refine Submodule.mem_iSup_of_mem d₁ (Submodule.mem_iSup_of_mem hd₁N ?_)
    refine ⟨CuspForm.levelRaise d₂ (Gamma1_map_le_conjAct_scaleGL_of_dvd hd₂M)
      f.primitiveAssociate.toCuspForm, ?_⟩
    rw [CuspForm.levelRaiseₗ_apply, CuspForm.levelRaise_levelRaise]
  · exact fun hmem ↦ f.conductor_dvd_of_mem_span_newform
      (Newform.iSup_range_levelRaise_le_span_levelRaise hmem)

/-- **The conductor is the least divisor level from which a good Hecke eigenform arises.** -/
theorem isLeast_conductor [NeZero N] (f : EigenformAwayFromLevel N k) :
    IsLeast {M : ℕ | ∃ _ : NeZero M, M ∣ N ∧
      f.toCuspForm ∈ ⨆ (d : ℕ) (hd : d * M ∣ N),
        haveI : NeZero d := NeZero.of_dvd (dvd_of_mul_right_dvd hd)
        LinearMap.range
          (CuspForm.levelRaiseₗ (k := k) d (Gamma1_map_le_conjAct_scaleGL_of_dvd hd))}
      f.conductor := by
  refine ⟨⟨inferInstance, f.conductor_dvd,
    (f.conductor_dvd_iff_mem_iSup_levelRaise f.conductor_dvd).mp dvd_rfl⟩, ?_⟩
  rintro M ⟨hM0, hMN, hmem⟩
  have := hM0
  exact Nat.le_of_dvd (NeZero.pos M) ((f.conductor_dvd_iff_mem_iSup_levelRaise hMN).mpr hmem)

/-! ### Stability under level-raising and bad-prime perturbations -/

/-- **Every nonzero form in the level-raise span of `f` has the same conductor as `f`.** -/
@[simp]
theorem conductor_ofMemSpanLevelRaise [NeZero M] [NeZero N] (f : EigenformAwayFromLevel M k)
    (hMN : M ∣ N) {F : CuspForm ((Gamma1 N).map (mapGL ℝ)) k}
    (hF : F ∈ Submodule.span ℂ {G : CuspForm ((Gamma1 N).map (mapGL ℝ)) k |
      ∃ (d : ℕ) (_ : NeZero d) (h : d * M ∣ N),
        CuspForm.levelRaise d (Gamma1_map_le_conjAct_scaleGL_of_dvd h) f.toCuspForm = G})
    (hF0 : F ≠ 0) :
    (f.ofMemSpanLevelRaise hMN hF hF0).conductor = f.conductor :=
  (conductor_eq_and_coe_primitiveAssociate_eq_of_forall_notMem_prime_eigenvalue_eq
    (f.ofMemSpanLevelRaise hMN hF hF0) f dvd_rfl hMN (by simp) (S := ∅) fun p hp hpN hpM _ ↦
      f.ofMemSpanLevelRaise_eigenvalue hMN hF hF0 ⟨p, hp.pos⟩ hpN hpM).1

/-- **Every nonzero form in the level-raise span of `f` has the same primitive associate as
`f`.** -/
@[simp]
theorem coe_primitiveAssociate_ofMemSpanLevelRaise [NeZero M] [NeZero N]
    (f : EigenformAwayFromLevel M k) (hMN : M ∣ N)
    {F : CuspForm ((Gamma1 N).map (mapGL ℝ)) k}
    (hF : F ∈ Submodule.span ℂ {G : CuspForm ((Gamma1 N).map (mapGL ℝ)) k |
      ∃ (d : ℕ) (_ : NeZero d) (h : d * M ∣ N),
        CuspForm.levelRaise d (Gamma1_map_le_conjAct_scaleGL_of_dvd h) f.toCuspForm = G})
    (hF0 : F ≠ 0) :
    ⇑(f.ofMemSpanLevelRaise hMN hF hF0).primitiveAssociate.toCuspForm =
      ⇑f.primitiveAssociate.toCuspForm :=
  (conductor_eq_and_coe_primitiveAssociate_eq_of_forall_notMem_prime_eigenvalue_eq
    (f.ofMemSpanLevelRaise hMN hF hF0) f dvd_rfl hMN (by simp) (S := ∅) fun p hp hpN hpM _ ↦
      f.ofMemSpanLevelRaise_eigenvalue hMN hF hF0 ⟨p, hp.pos⟩ hpN hpM).2

/-- **Invariance of the conductor under level-raising.** -/
@[simp]
theorem conductor_levelRaise [NeZero M] [NeZero N] (d : ℕ) [NeZero d] (h : d * M ∣ N)
    (f : EigenformAwayFromLevel M k) :
    (f.levelRaise d h).conductor = f.conductor :=
  (conductor_eq_and_coe_primitiveAssociate_eq_of_forall_notMem_prime_eigenvalue_eq
    (f.levelRaise d h) f dvd_rfl (dvd_of_mul_left_dvd h) (by simp) (S := ∅)
    fun p hp hpN hpM _ ↦ f.levelRaise_eigenvalue d h ⟨p, hp.pos⟩ hpN hpM).1

/-- **Invariance of the primitive associate under level-raising.** -/
@[simp]
theorem coe_primitiveAssociate_levelRaise [NeZero M] [NeZero N] (d : ℕ) [NeZero d]
    (h : d * M ∣ N) (f : EigenformAwayFromLevel M k) :
    ⇑(f.levelRaise d h).primitiveAssociate.toCuspForm = ⇑f.primitiveAssociate.toCuspForm :=
  (conductor_eq_and_coe_primitiveAssociate_eq_of_forall_notMem_prime_eigenvalue_eq
    (f.levelRaise d h) f dvd_rfl (dvd_of_mul_left_dvd h) (by simp) (S := ∅)
    fun p hp hpN hpM _ ↦ f.levelRaise_eigenvalue d h ⟨p, hp.pos⟩ hpN hpM).2

end EigenformAwayFromLevel

namespace Newform

/-- **Bad-prime Fourier coefficients are unconstrained by the good eigensystem.** For any newform
`g` of level `M`, any divisor `d > 1` with `d * M ∣ N`, and any complex number `w`, there exists a
normalised good Hecke eigenform at level `N` whose conductor is `M`, whose primitive associate is
`g`, and whose `d`-th Fourier coefficient is `w`. -/
theorem exists_eigenformAwayFromLevel_qExpansion_coeff_eq [NeZero M] [NeZero N] (g : Newform M k)
    {d : ℕ} (hd1 : 1 < d) (hd : d * M ∣ N) (w : ℂ) :
    ∃ f : EigenformAwayFromLevel N k,
      (qExpansion 1 f.toCuspForm).coeff 1 = 1 ∧
      f.conductor = M ∧
      ⇑f.primitiveAssociate.toCuspForm = ⇑g.toCuspForm ∧
      (qExpansion 1 f.toCuspForm).coeff d = w := by
  have : NeZero d := ⟨(zero_lt_one.trans hd1).ne'⟩
  have hMN : M ∣ N := dvd_of_mul_left_dvd hd
  have h₁ : 1 * M ∣ N := (one_mul M).symm ▸ hMN
  -- Construct `F = V₁ g + (w - a_d(g)) • V_d g` in the level-raise span of `g`.
  let c : ℂ := w - (qExpansion 1 g.toCuspForm).coeff d
  let F : CuspForm ((Gamma1 N).map (mapGL ℝ)) k :=
    CuspForm.levelRaise 1 (Gamma1_map_le_conjAct_scaleGL_of_dvd h₁) g.toCuspForm +
      c • CuspForm.levelRaise d (Gamma1_map_le_conjAct_scaleGL_of_dvd hd) g.toCuspForm
  have hΓM := one_mem_strictPeriods_Gamma1_map M
  have hΓN := one_mem_strictPeriods_Gamma1_map N
  have hcoeff (n : ℕ) : (qExpansion 1 F).coeff n =
      (qExpansion 1 g.toCuspForm).coeff n +
        c * if d ∣ n then (qExpansion 1 g.toCuspForm).coeff (n / d) else 0 := by
    have hlin := map_add (CuspForm.qExpansionCoeffₗ one_pos hΓN k n)
      (CuspForm.levelRaise 1 (Gamma1_map_le_conjAct_scaleGL_of_dvd h₁) g.toCuspForm)
      (c • CuspForm.levelRaise d (Gamma1_map_le_conjAct_scaleGL_of_dvd hd) g.toCuspForm)
    rw [_root_.map_smul, smul_eq_mul, CuspForm.qExpansionCoeffₗ_apply,
      CuspForm.qExpansionCoeffₗ_apply, CuspForm.qExpansionCoeffₗ_apply,
      CuspForm.qExpansion_levelRaise_coeff hΓM, CuspForm.qExpansion_levelRaise_coeff hΓM] at hlin
    simpa only [one_dvd, ↓reduceIte, Nat.div_one] using hlin
  have hc1 : (qExpansion 1 F).coeff 1 = 1 := by
    simp [hcoeff, Nat.not_dvd_of_pos_of_lt zero_lt_one hd1]
  have hF0 : F ≠ 0 := fun h0 ↦ zero_ne_one <| by
    rwa [← CuspForm.qExpansionCoeffₗ_apply one_pos hΓN, h0, map_zero] at hc1
  have hcd : (qExpansion 1 F).coeff d = w := by
    simp [hcoeff, Nat.div_self (zero_lt_one.trans hd1), c]
  have hmem : F ∈ Submodule.span ℂ {G : CuspForm ((Gamma1 N).map (mapGL ℝ)) k |
      ∃ (e : ℕ) (_ : NeZero e) (h : e * M ∣ N),
        CuspForm.levelRaise e (Gamma1_map_le_conjAct_scaleGL_of_dvd h) g.toCuspForm = G} :=
    add_mem (Submodule.subset_span ⟨1, inferInstance, h₁, rfl⟩)
      (Submodule.smul_mem _ c (Submodule.subset_span ⟨d, inferInstance, hd, rfl⟩))
  refine ⟨g.toEigenformAwayFromLevel.ofMemSpanLevelRaise hMN hmem hF0, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · simpa only [EigenformAwayFromLevel.ofMemSpanLevelRaise_toCuspForm] using hc1
  · simp
  · simp
  · simpa only [EigenformAwayFromLevel.ofMemSpanLevelRaise_toCuspForm] using hcd

end Newform

end HeckeRing.GL2

